Use media export when you need the image, audio, or video files themselves—for
a grant report, permit report, presentation, or colleague who does not use
NAHPU.

You can export one file with full control over dimensions and quality, or
export a multi-file selection as a single archive. Audio and video can be
included in a selection, while conversion and resizing apply to images only.

## Export a single file

Open any media item and select `Export` {% ref id="G" /%} to open `Export media`
(shown as a bottom sheet on phones and a dialog on wider screens).

{% steps %}

1. Review `File name` {% ref id="E" /%}. NAHPU suggests the current filename;
   turn on `Append date` {% ref id="F" /%} to add today's date.
2. Choose a file format {% ref id="D" /%}. `Original` is always available;
   `JPEG`, `PNG`, and `WebP` appear when NAHPU can decode the image (`.jpg`,
   `.jpeg`, `.png`, and `.webp` sources).
3. When exporting to `JPEG`, `PNG`, or `WebP`, turn on `Resize image` if you
   want a smaller file. Aspect ratio is locked so editing width updates height,
   and neither dimension can exceed the original size shown above the switch.
4. For `JPEG`, adjust `JPEG quality` (default `85%` balances detail and size;
   lower values suit email or slow uploads).
5. Choose a destination folder on desktop and select `Export`. Once written,
   you can `Share`, open the folder, or save a copy.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="note" %}

Files NAHPU cannot decode—such as camera RAW files—still export in their
`Original` format; conversion and resizing controls are hidden.

{% /aside %}

## Export a selection as an archive

Open `Media gallery` {% ref id="A" /%} from the home screen menu (to browse
media across all projects) or from any record's media panel, or select files
directly inside a record's media panel. Enable selection {% ref id="B" /%},
pick your files, and select `Export` to open `Export selected media` {% ref id="C" /%}.

`Archive contents` summarizes how many files were selected, how many were found
on disk, counts by media type (images, audio, video, other), total
`Source size`, and warnings for missing or unconvertible files.

Configure the archive under `Archive`:

| Setting | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| Archive format | Choose `TAR.GZ` (default) or `ZIP` based on the recipient's tools. |
| `Image format` | `Original` copies images unchanged; `JPEG`, `PNG`, or `WebP` converts every readable image. |
| `Limit image dimensions` | Shown when converting: caps the longer side to a maximum pixel size without upscaling smaller images. |
| `JPEG quality` | Shown when converting to `JPEG` (default `85%`). |
| `File name` and `Append date` | Sets the archive name (and optionally appends today's date). |

Inside the archive, files are organized into `specimen`, `site`, `event`,
`narrative`, and `other` folders. Audio and video files are always copied
unchanged.

{% aside type="caution" %}

Large batches—especially with image conversion—can take several minutes. Keep
NAHPU open while progress runs (use `Cancel` if you need to stop), then check
the exported count, skipped count, and warnings before sharing the archive.

{% /aside %}

## Choosing settings

| Use | Format | Size | JPEG quality |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Archiving or further editing | `Original` | Unchanged | — |
| Printed report or poster | `JPEG` or `PNG` | Large enough for print dimensions | 85–95% |
| Slides or web page | `JPEG` or `WebP` | ~2000 px on the long side | 80–85% |
| Email or slow upload | `JPEG` | ~1200 px on the long side | 70–80% |

Inspect a sample exported image at its intended viewing size before sharing a
batch. Resizing and JPEG compression permanently discard detail, so keep the
original files.

